>rub weed on wound
You gently press the limp weed against the wounded wing.
  The pterodactyl's sleep seems to deepen, and the tension in its limbs relaxes. You watch in astonishment as the weed begins to flow and congeal, blending itself into the torn flesh until no trace of the wound remains.
  The pterodactyl snorts restlessly. It looks as if it's about to wake up.

>drop arrow
You drop the arrow.
  The pterodactyl shakes its head, blinks its eyes and yawns stupidly.

>
