>kiss horn
The unicorn backs away; but not before you touch her horn with your lips.
  [Your luck just went up.]
  The unicorn whinnies sadly.

>give chest to unicorn
You drop the sea chest over the side of the stall, where it falls with a heavy CLUNK.
  The unicorn cranes her neck towards the sea chest and snuffles the lid curiously. She whinnies with joy and nuzzles your face with shy gratitude. Then, eyes bright with anticipation, the lovely creature prods the lid of the chest with her nose.
  Rays of golden light burst from the sea chest's interior as the lid creaks open. The unicorn is bathed in a chorus of radiant ecstasy that almost drowns out the telltale snap of an opening Gate.
  When your head clears, the unicorn is gone without a trace.
  [Your compassion just went up.]

