  The beast behind the oak tree makes itself as small as possible.

>wait
Time passes.
  "Hide from me, will ye, ye snufflin' she-devil!" cries the hunter striding back into the forest. "It's to the hounds I'll be throwin' yer bleedin' carcass!" His curses soon fade into the distance.
  The minx pokes its nose out from behind the oak tree, sniffing fearfully. It peeks around the corner, and its brown eyes lock with yours.
  "Minx?"

