>blow whistle
The whistle emits a long, harsh wail.
  Nothing happens for a moment. Then, with a raucous cry and a great beating of wings, the pterodactyl lands by your side.
  This is the first time I have answered the whistle's call, observes a voice in your head. Twice more you may use it to summon me. I wait at your disposal.

