>blow whistle
The whistle emits a long, harsh wail.
  Nothing happens for a moment. Then, with a raucous cry and a great beating of wings, the pterodactyl lands by your side.
  This is the last time I shall answer the whistle's call, observes a voice in your head; and as it speaks, the whistle melts away into nothingness. I wait at your disposal.

