>blow bubble
You dip the circlet in the crystal jar, draw it out and blow into the swirling film.
  A silvery bubble blows out of the circlet! You watch as it flattens into a perfectly circular mirror, rotating more and more slowly until it faces northeast.
  "How droll," remarks the shadow.
  A sunbeam is reflected northeast.
  The shadow's chuckling subsides. "I rarely get visitors," it admits in a wistful tone. "A pity I have to destroy you."

